Accounts

every cooperator holds Six (6) seperate savings accounts

1. Wallet savings account      wallet_thrift_account, wallet_authorization_breakdown, wallet_savings_account
2. Scheme savings account      scheme_authorization_breakdown, scheme_savings_account

3. Loans savings account
4. Loans buffer savings account

5. Commodities savings account
6. Commodities buffer savings account


the buffer accounts are important because cooperators can sometimes pay cash for any of their obligations



your wallet account balance at any given time should be the sum 
of the balances from all six accounts



My savings Module
This module is summerised thus.
A cooperator instructs the accountant to
deduct a fixed amount of money from their salary and 
hand same to the manager of the cooperative, who then deposits it into their ( the cooperator's) WALLET or SCHEME SAVINGS ACCOUNT with the cooperative


Proration Table
there should be one table which holds all pending and executed deductions. On proration, the differnt accounts
are filled with appropriate entries




VALUE ADDED SERVICES
This amount should be editable at any given time


MODELS
The wallet savings account should have the following flags
1. can get loan
2. can buy commodities


BY DEFAULTS
when a new cooperator is onboarded, these flags are both turned off by default, 
the manager would have to turn them on for you (the cooperator)




CYCLE OF EVENTS
1. A written authorization / mandate
2. Proration



